    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core led by **Gunnar Henderson** (76.04) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). Despite facing the formidable arm of Cole, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to an elite 16% park factor and the inherent power-speed upside he provides in the #3 hole. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** presents perhaps the most favorable statistical profile of the day; he benefits from a 16% park boost against Bradish and a 14% dynamic platoon advantage, making him the anchor of our infield production. **Heliot Ramos** (67.47) also draws a strong start in the same matchup, though his upside is slightly tempered by the fact that Bradish is an elite hold against the stolen base, which penalizes his speed-dependent profile.\n\nOur outfield is anchored by the table-setting speed of **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Wade Meckler** (53.18). **Sam Antonacci** earns a significant edge against Holmes due to a 17% SP skill advantage, providing a solid floor for our R/SB production. Conversely, **Luis Lara** (41.15) sits near the bottom of our efficiency threshold; his #9 lineup placement creates a drag on his overall output, though his utility as a switch-hitter keeps him marginally playable. **Miguel Vargas** (58.99) falls just short of the 60+ \"Strong\" category, but remains a viable play given his strong xwOBA metrics against the Holmes matchup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster today was benching **Nasim Nunez** (39.47), who narrowly missed our 40-point start threshold. While **Nasim Nunez** provides essential speed, he is facing the elite arm of deGrom, whose high strikeout floor creates a significant negative SP skill adjustment (-19%). This matchup, compounded by the 50% stolen base suppression typically seen against elite arms, forced the optimizer to keep him on the bench. We are also managing the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages**, who are all sidelined by team off-days, further limiting our flexibility in today\u2019s 5x5 Roto chase.",
